+# Supply Chain & Evidence Runbook (operators)
+
+This runbook describes steps to harden supply chain, enable cosign with KMS, configure webhook TLS via cert-manager and ensure immutable evidence retention.
+
+1) Provision KMS and S3
+ - Run terraform in terraform/kms_and_s3 with required vars:
+     terraform init && terraform apply -var="evidence_bucket_name=aegis-evidence" -var="aws_region=us-west-2"
+ - Note outputs: cosign_kms_key_arn and evidence_bucket
+
+2) Store KMS ARN in Kubernetes
+ - ./ops/cosign/attach_kms_secret.sh <COSIGN_KMS_ARN> security
+
+3) Deploy cosign admission webhook with Cert-Manager
+ - Install cert-manager
+ - helm upgrade --install cosign-admission helm/cosign-admission -n admission --create-namespace --set tls.enableCertManager=true --set tls.secretName=cosign-webhook-tls
+ - Wait for certificate issuance, then populate CA bundle:
+     ./ops/cosign/populate_ca_bundle.sh admission cosign-webhook-tls cosign-validating-webhook
+
+4) Configure CI secrets
+ - Add COSIGN_AWS_KMS_KEY_ARN to GitHub Actions secrets
+ - Ensure KUBECONFIG secret present for CI jobs that verify deployment
+
+5) Evidence ingestion
+ - Deploy ops/s3/event_uploader.py as a daemonset mounting /var/log/aegis to stream logs to S3 evidence bucket
+ - Ensure bucket has Object Lock enabled and default retention per legal requirement
+
+6) Test & Validate
+ - Run .github/workflows/promotion_cr_test.yml to create a ModelPromotion CR and ensure controller performs expected verification and promotion steps (including rollback on failure)
+ - Run ops/cosign/ci_sign_verify_deploy.yml to validate signed and unsigned image admission behavior
+
